    - name: modelReasoningTextResult
      type: object
      samples:
      - '"**Analyzing the `$NOW` Filter Detection Logic**\n\nOkay, so I''m looking
        at this `filterHasNow` function, which is designed to identify if a given
        Directus filter utilizes the `$NOW` dynamic variable. The input is a `Filter`
        object (from the `@directus/types` package), and the output is a boolean indicating
        the presence or absence of `$NOW`.\n\nThe core of the problem seems to be
        the recursive nature of these filters. They can be deeply nested structures,
        using logical operators like `_and` and `_or`, along with field names and
        comparison operators (`_gt`, `_lt`, etc.). The key is, of course, the string
        literal `''$NOW''`.\n\nMy strategy here is pretty straightforward: I''ll iterate
        through the keys of the filter object. If a value is *exactly* `''$NOW''`,
        then I immediately return `true`. If the value is an array, meaning it''s
        a logical grouping like an `_and` or `_or`, I''ll recursively call `filterHasNow`
